  "scientific_interpretation": "The frozen physical Nc groups are all well represented, so a missing or severely depleted high-Nc training group is not the explanation. Both COMP-XPU-002 and COMP-XPU-003 show systematically sub-unity model-to-teacher Nc response gains in both source cases, including front-excluded diagnostics. Simple Nc input scaling increases some response gains but does not solve the relative high-Nc weakness. The next controlled hypothesis is therefore that the recurrent model needs the known compressibility coordinate stretch exposed explicitly as a sequence feature rather than relying on the LSTM to infer it from the scalar conditioner.",
  "why_not_weighting_first": "Per-Nc losses increase with Nc, but the sample groups are already represented and the audit directly demonstrates insufficient profile response to Nc. A fixed high-Nc loss multiplier would require choosing a new weighting magnitude without a source-prescribed value. The physics-aware coordinate channel tests the observed response deficiency without inventing a loss coefficient.",
  "not_concluded": [
    "loss weighting can never help",
